287 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 265 0 R
/E (The energy generated by a solar photovoltaic \(PV\) panel depends on its tilt and azimuth angles, which vary according to the geographical location. Selecting suitable angles manually can be time-consuming and may not provide the maximum possible annual energy yield.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
288 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 265 0 R
/E (Therefore, there is a need for a system that can automatically determine the optimal tilt and azimuth angles for a given location. The proposed system uses geocoding to obtain the location coordinates, PVGIS to estimate annual solar energy yield, and Hill Climbing and Simulated Annealing algorithms to search for an orientation that maximizes energy generation.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
